{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact formal candidate 13e704a47a409a47e14cdc24a00520735168ee98 on codex/formal-state-machines-20261108, all 38 paths, for request 3c6d197d under promise 5c826d74 and review request 689c5831. Five skills, five bounded TLA+ models, five charts and five source witnesses describe source at 8faa38dc. Their hashes match main cdd5508c. Every model, model fault and source control gives its recorded result. The head cannot land as it stands: its single gate failed, the branch is not on origin, and the four changes below are required.\n\nRequired:\n\n1. Gate. The single gate at this head ended with exit 1. The recovered Node owner and the three unreached stages ran separately and do not make a passing gate. Run one fresh `npm run gate` at the final head, from the formal worktree, in its turn for the validation slot.\n2. Push. origin has no codex/formal-state-machines-20261108. Push the final head before its review request.\n3. Source controls. control.mjs writes the fault into the checkout that runs it. The earlier driver did the same in ~/play/artroom, and the Transport fault there broke the gate's Node stage. Make control.mjs refuse to start when `git status --porcelain` lists any change. In the README and in each skill, state two rules:\n   - Run check.mjs and control.mjs only from a dedicated worktree, never from ~/play/artroom.\n   - Run them only while holding the single validation slot (ruling 1b14c28a).\n4. Editor model and chart. The model gives \"Checking receipt\" one exit, `Verify`, so the chart shows every accepted request reaching \"Receipt verified\". In the source, a failed `verifyStep` keeps the accepted step unadvanced, with \"The acceptance could not be verified; the task stays unknown.\" (retained-editor-data.ts lines 200 and 277). That path is the case the model exists for. Add an action that leaves an accepted, unverified edit unadvanced, and count that state as terminal for the deadlock check. Then regenerate