nsport witness drives a real `HttpGeneration`. The Editor witness drives the real `transitionEdit`.\n- Evidence. The manifest hashes to c509ce51…, the value that the request cites. Its 294 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match.\n- Charts. The five SVGs contain no script, event handler or link. Their only URL is the SVG namespace.\n\nArchitecture: one change needed (item 3). Each subsystem keeps its model, view, coverage record and source witness side by side. check.mjs refuses drift and a TLC jar with the wrong digest before it runs anything. The control runner is the one part that can damage another lane's work, because it edits product source in place.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Nothing changes product behavior. The scripts read repository files, run tests and run TLC from a jar checked by SHA-256. No credential appears in the files or the evidence.\n\nSimplification: no required change beyond item 4. Each invariant restates the guard of one action, so TLC confirms that guard rather than an ordering result. The regression protection comes from the five source witnesses and their controls. The models contribute the charts and the review checklist. Say that plainly in the README beside \"TLC 1.7.4 exhaustively explored each finite model\". The note's command column also names /tmp scripts and \"/statechart with the retained model and view\". Name the retained copies in the evidence directory instead, because /tmp does not keep them.\n\nThis verdict authorizes no landing or deployment and closes no live acceptance.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e14cf3aa5fdddabe791d927fd02d193834d83aa4","binding":"assigned","head":"13e704a47a409a47e14cdc24a00520735168ee98","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e16570ddd48279770c0c692f5612000daa532486\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1